Quad4 smart fork of Forgejo
===========================

Remotes
  upstream  https://codeberg.org/forgejo/forgejo.git  (fetch only, push disabled)
  origin    git@github.com:Quad4-Software/forge.git

Branches
  forgejo   tracks upstream/forgejo (clean Forgejo tip, do not commit here)
  master    Quad4 customizations (default)

Sync upstream
  git checkout master
  contrib/quad4/sync-upstream.sh
  or wait for .github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml weekly PR

Branding
  Default theme: quad4-dark
  Theme source: web_src/css/themes/theme-quad4-dark.css
  Logo masters: contrib/quad4/brand/quad4-mark*.svg + source-mark.png
  Rebuild: contrib/quad4/rebuild-brand.sh

DevOps platform features
  Bot protection: RavenGuard edge (ALTCHA removed)
  Optional external Sentry/GlitchTip DSN via [sentry] (not shipped in compose)
  Public OSINT hardening: footer Powered by / Version / Page / Template only for
  signed-in users. GET /api/v1/version requires auth. Anonymous pages stay silent.

Notifications (no SMTP, no email)
  Outbound email/SMTP and incoming email are removed. Account activation,
  password reset, security notices, issue/PR activity, releases, repo
  transfers, team invites and admin notices are delivered over LXMF to
  Reticulum identities registered on the account.
  Requires [rns] ENABLED=true and ENABLE_LXMF=true. When LXMF is available,
  signup requires a Reticulum identity hash and the account starts inactive
  until the delivered activation link is used.
  services/mailer keeps the notifier API; Message/SendAsync dispatch over
  LXMF via services/lxmfnotify. Security notices and invites to existing
  users go to verified identities only.
  Users still have a placeholder email column (name@NO_REPLY_ADDRESS) for
  model/API compatibility, but nothing is delivered to it. Password reset
  resolves by username or Reticulum identity hash.
  Users manage identities under /user/settings/rns_keys.

Secure setup link
  While INSTALL_LOCK is false the install page is gated by a token:
  custom/setup-token (mode 0600) holds a 256 bit token plus a 1h expiry.
  Startup prints "http://host/?key=..." to stdout only, never to the log.
  GET / needs ?key=, POST / needs the hidden setup_key form field. Wrong or
  expired keys get a 403 page pointing at the regenerate command:
    forge admin regenerate-setup-link
  Regeneration works against a running server, the token file is re-read per
  request. Successful install deletes the token. Routers: routers/install/setup.go.

QA gates
  make test-qa    runs the page-matrix axe scan plus Lighthouse CI.
  tests/e2e/pages-a11y.test.e2e.ts  scans 24 seeded pages (anon + auth) and
    fails on new violation rules or counts above tests/e2e/pages-a11y-baseline.json.
    Regenerate baseline: UPDATE_A11Y_BASELINE=1 plus the same test run.
    Matrix is pinned to the chromium project for a stable baseline.
  tests/e2e/lighthouse_test.go    RUN_LIGHTHOUSE=1 gate, boots the seeded
    server and runs npx lhci autorun with lighthouserc.cjs. Reports land in
    tests/e2e/reports/lhci (filesystem target, nothing uploaded).
    Accessibility floor 0.8, raise it as baseline violations get fixed.
  .github/workflows/qa.yml        CI job for both, zizmor clean.

Compose
  docker-compose.yml           hardened stack: RavenGuard edge -> forge + postgres + Valkey
  docker-compose.coolify.yml   Coolify: SERVICE_URL_* only on ravenguard:8080
  deploy/ravenguard/           ravenguard.toml (local edge), ravenguard.coolify.toml (behind Coolify)
  .env.example                 copy to .env
  Valkey: cache/session/queue via rediss://default:pass@valkey:6379 (TLS + auth)
  SurrealDB optional: surreal://user:pass@host:8000/ns/db (modules/nosql/surreal.go)
  Hardening: no-new-privileges, cap_drop ALL (postgres gets minimal cap_add), healthchecks
  Internal TLS: pki-init (one-shot, openssl from the valkey image) issues an
    internal CA plus server certs for db and valkey into the forge-pki volume.
    The CA private key never leaves the init container tmpfs.
    Postgres: ssl=on, certs from /pki, custom pg_hba.conf requires hostssl +
    scram-sha-256 for all network conns (local socket stays trust for
    initdb/healthcheck). Forge uses SSL_MODE=verify-full.
    Valkey: TLS-only listener (--port 0 --tls-port 6379), requirepass auth,
    tls-auth-clients no. Forge uses rediss:// URIs with the default user.
    Forge trusts the CA via SSL_CERT_DIR=/etc/ssl/certs:/pki (forge-ca volume
    carries only ca.crt). Verified live: TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 on forge pg
    conns, wrong password/plaintext/missing CA all rejected.
    Rotation: to re-issue certs, remove forge-pki + forge-ca volumes and let
    pki-init regenerate; restart the stack.
    Required secrets: FORGE_DB_PASSWORD, VALKEY_PASSWORD, RG_CHALLENGE_SECRET.
  RavenGuard: https://github.com/Quad4-Software/ravenguard (standalone edge, not hub proxy mode)
  Coolify: assign domain to ravenguard only. Forge ROOT_URL reuses SERVICE_URL_RAVENGUARD_8080.

Crow CI
  docker-compose.crow.yml    standalone Crow v6.9.0 stack (digest-pinned
    codefloe.com/crowci/crow-server + crow-agent). Separate deploy, talks to
    Forge over public URLs only: webhooks forge -> crow, API/OAuth crow -> forge.
    Setup: create a Forge OAuth2 app with redirect ${CROW_HOST}/authorize,
    set CROW_HOST FORGEJO_URL CROW_FORGEJO_CLIENT/SECRET CROW_AGENT_SECRET.
    Coolify: add as its own Docker Compose resource, domain on crow:8000.
    Agent mounts /var/run/docker.sock = host-root equivalent, CI jobs host only.

DevOps companions (optional next)
  Prefer behind RavenGuard or private network. Catalog: https://selfh.st/apps/
  CI: Forgejo Actions runner, or Woodpecker CI
  Registry: Zot (light OCI) or Harbor (full featured)
  Objects/LFS: Garage or SeaweedFS (S3-compatible; avoid unmaintained MinIO)
  Secrets: OpenBao or Infisical
  Auth: Authentik or Keycloak (OIDC into Forge)
  Observability: Prometheus + Grafana (Forge metrics already optional)
  Deps: Renovate bot against the forge
  Status: Uptime Kuma
  See also sovereign CI notes: Forgejo + Woodpecker + Zot

